mode: "100644"
text: "# Design tools 2026 — verified\n\n*Design fundamentals (hierarchy, contrast, legibility) are timeless. The TOOLS move — re-verify quarterly.*\n\n## The POV: consistency + speed beat bespoke\nFor social, the win isn't one beautiful design — it's **six versions that still look like the same\ncampaign**, produced fast by a non-designer. The lever is a **small reusable template system anchored in a\nbrand kit**, which prevents both **brand drift** and generic **\"template energy.\"** \"Boring is repeatable.\"\nThe honest ceiling: these tools get you **~70–80% on-brand** — a human eye still finishes the hero work.\n\n## The tools (verify-quarterly)\n- **Canva (Magic Studio)** — the **social-first default** for non-designers (260M+ users). **Brand Kit**\n  (upload colors/fonts/logos once → auto-applies, kills brand drift) · **Magic Design** (layouts from a\n  prompt/brand kit) · **Magic Switch / Magic Resize** (one design → all platform sizes without rebuilding) ·\n  **Magic Write** (in-canvas copy) · **Dream Lab** (marketing-tuned image gen + style transfer) · **Bulk\n  Create** (CSV → many designs) · **Canva Sheets → Magic Charts** (data → branded charts). **Pro ~$15/mo**\n  (~$120/yr). **Honest limits:** recognizably **\"Canva-style\"** at the ceiling; **AI credit limits**; raw AI\n  generations **generally not copyrightable** (US/EU); **\"Canva Shield\" indemnification on Enterprise only.**\n- **Adobe Express (+ Firefly)** — between Figma's complexity + Canva's simplicity. **Firefly** is trained on\n  **licensed content → brand-safe + IP indemnification**; higher-quality, more controllable imagery; Adobe\n  ecosystem. The \"most consistent performer\" in 2026 tests. Pick it for **premium imagery + IP assurance.**\n- **Figma** — master **design systems / brand governance / UI** (component-based); the brand \"source of\n  truth\" for larger teams; **not** ideal for daily social graphics (context-switching cost). (State of the\n  Designer 2026: 72% of designers use generative AI; 91% say it improves quality.)\n- **Adjacent:** **Microsoft Designer** (DALL·E-based, M365), **Gamma** (AI decks/sites), **Visme**\n  (infographics/data-viz).\n\n## The \"combine, don't pick one\" insight\nAssign each tool to its **strength zone**: **Canva** for speed/volume + day-to-day social; **Adobe Express/\nFirefly** for premium, brand-safe, indemnified imagery; **Figma** for the master system + governance. Most\nsocial-first SMB/creator teams → **Canva is the obvious default**, with the image tools (`image-prompt`) or\nFirefly for the hero visuals.\n\n## Relationship to the image tools (the library's generative branch)\nThis skill is about **layout + template systems** (type, hierarchy, brand consistency, reusable frames) —\noften **not generative.** When a template needs a **generated image**, brief the image tools (`image-prompt`\n→ `ideogram` for text-in-image, `nano-banana` for photoreal + edits/composition, `flux` for\nedit control + character/product consistency, Midjourney for artistic)\nor use a built-in generator (Canva **Dream Lab** / Adobe **Firefly**). Layout ≠ generation — they connect.\n"
